  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated HIV, Water and Sanitation Project - JOAC St Alberts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">St Albert&apos;s in Centenary is situated in Agro-economic Region 5 in Zimbabwe and experiences critical water shortages in its communities and at the Mission Hospital. The communities it serves are very poor communities that have suffered heavily on the impact of HIV and AIDS, early marriages due to poverty and cases of skin diseases,  diarrhoeal, and other water bone diseases.
This project aims at improving the water and sanitation and hygiene standards for vulnerable communities in Centenary and Muzarabani. The primary focus will be for pregnant and expectant mothers at the shelter and provide with improved latrines, bathing facilities and solar driven borehole and water pumping system the project will benefit over seven thousand people accessing the facilities and reached out to through awareness raising on basic hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
